[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axis enumeration (what the C actually branches on)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 1 — public entry points (the FULL set, lowest level included)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `nm -D --defined-only c_src/build/libdriver.so` gives one strong symbol, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c_src/include/driver.h` declares one prototype:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m void driver(int x);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is therefore exactly **one** public entry point, and it *is* the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m lowest-level one — there is no convenience/one-shot wrapper layered over a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m lower-level API, and no `static` internal helper that a wrapper composes. No
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m context/handle object exists, so there is no setup-then-run pipeline to drive.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axis 1 has a single value: `driver`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 2 — runtime options / modes / flags
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `grep -nE 'if|switch|#if|else|enum|struct|typedef|extern|global|static' c_src/src/driver.c c_src/include/driver.h`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m returns only the `DRIVER_H_` include guard. The header exposes no setter, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m option struct, no flags parameter, and no global variable; the `.so` exports no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m data symbols (`nm -D --defined-only` shows no `B`/`D`/`R` entries). There is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **no runtime option and no compile-time `#ifdef` configuration** to toggle.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axis 2 has a single value: *none*.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 3 — input shape / value class
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The only input is one `int` passed by value. There is no size, count, width,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m element type, format, byte order, or emptiness axis — no buffer, no length, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m array. What the C *does* distinguish on that `int` is the arithmetic and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `%d` conversion:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `2*x` — wraps (two's complement) once `|x| > INT_MAX/2`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `y += 300` — wraps once `2*x > INT_MAX - 300`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `printf("%d\n", y)` — glibc's `%d` branches on `y`'s sign (emits `-` or not),
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   on `y == 0` (special-cased digit emission), and on the decimal digit count
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (1..10 digits) when converting.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Giving these value classes: zero, small ±, the exact `y == 0` preimage
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`x == -150`), sign-flip neighbourhood of `y`, every decimal-digit-count
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m boundary of `y`, the `2*x` overflow boundary, the `+300` overflow boundary, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the domain extremes `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 4 — observable output channel state
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `driver` has no return value; its **entire** observable effect is bytes written
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m to the process's `stdout` via libc `printf`. A real consumer's `stdout` is in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m one of glibc's three buffering modes, and the consumer interleaves its own
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m stdio writes with calls into the library. Buffering mode and interleaving are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m genuine state the code interacts with (writing via a different mechanism —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m e.g. Rust's `std::io::stdout`, which holds its own buffer — would reorder bytes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m relative to a C caller's writes while still producing the right bytes in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m isolation). Axis 4 values: fully buffered (redirected fd), line buffered,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m unbuffered, plus call-multiplicity (one call / many calls per flush) and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m interleaving with the caller's own `printf`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## CONFIGURATION-SURFACE TABLE
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Pruned cross-product of Axis 3 × Axis 4 (Axes 1 and 2 are single-valued).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every row is run against BOTH `.so`s through `libloading` and compared
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m byte-for-byte; rows marked *randomized* use many property-style inputs from a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m fixed-seed PRNG.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 | `driver` | options: none. `x == 0` (zero value) → `y == 300`; stdout fully buffered | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2 | `driver` | options: none. `x` small positive, `1..=1000` exhaustive; fully buffered | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 3 | `driver` | options: none. `x` small negative, `-1000..=-1` exhaustive; fully buffered | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 4 | `driver` | options: none. `x == -150`, the exact preimage of `y == 0` (`printf` zero special case); fully buffered | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 5 | `driver` | options: none. sign-flip neighbourhood of `y`: `x ∈ {-152,-151,-150,-149,-148}` (`y` crosses 0, `-` sign appears/disappears); fully buffered | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 6 | `driver` | options: none. every decimal-digit-count boundary of `y` (1→2→…→10 digits, both signs): `x` such that `y ∈ {±1,±9,±10,±99,±100,±999,±1000,…,±1000000000, INT_MAX, INT_MIN}`; fully buffered | [x] |
